help/contracts/dispatch aligned"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-ugqx"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A caller explicitly disabling a boolean option cannot silently enable it in an extension handler."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-gh1461","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-10-14T07:54:43.008Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-10-14T07:54:43.008Z","author":"harness:codex","text":"Duplicate check: full all-status corpus, fresh flag searches/open/in-progress reads; full closed normalization owner metadata/history confirms completed prior scope. GH1466 body/all comments read: exact-source comparison is reported evidence and published14 execution remains pending. No exact owner found; this follow-on remains open/unclaimed and does not reopen completed work."}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"9b8ce261d287d51068d0e93639fd4e38040ae27a0743e54ab8b0e2ffed63ff4a","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"ab6e75f77a2f02993e5f1de2161f74f3806e7f2e280ff115110be9c52928b560"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-14T07:56:00.352Z","author":"harness:codex","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"c55fa3824028333991367803","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"probe"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-26hybs","lineage:pm-26hybs","lineage:pm-gh1457","lineage:pm-f05lsg","lineage:pm-mpbb","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"pm-26hybs","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-26hybs","lineage:pm-26hybs","lineage:pm-gh1457","lineage:pm-f05lsg","lineage:pm-mpbb","lineage:pm-doxj"]}},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"Source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1466\n\n## Scope\nSource-proven compatibility regression in v2026.10.14 commit `2024387a346bb88e0590e07cb3262e03307b997b`, compared with `828edf4ae71d27c28a103ca05cec87366d88a5fd` and the verified installed 2026.10.13 artifact. **Published 10.14 artifact execution remains pending** because direct official npm access was unavailable. No mutating handler was exercised.\n\n## Minimal case\nA harmless extension command:\n```js\napi.registerCommand({\n  name: \"contract probe\",\n  flags: [{ long: \"--enabled\", type: \"bool\", default: true }],\n  run(context) {\n    return { options: context.options, args: context.args };\n  },\n});\n```\n\nInvocation: `pm contract probe --enabled false --json` (also `--enabled 0`).\n\n- Actual installed 10.13 invokes the echo handler with `enabled:false,args:[]`.\n- Exact old/new source composition changes the same argv from `enabled:false,args:[]` to **`enabled:true,args:[\"false\"]`**; `0` changes analogously.\n- A caller explicitly trying to disable the option can therefore supply the opposite option to the handler, depending on its accepted positional arguments.\n\n## Evidence\n[New scalar-kind normalization](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/2024387a346bb88e0590e07cb3262e03307b997b/src/cli/extension-command-help.ts#L202-L217) makes legacy `bool` a value-free Commander switch. The following literal becomes a positional argument. [Invocation extraction](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/2024387a346bb88e0590e07cb3262e03307b997b/src/cli/runtime/invocation-options.ts#L148-L210) retains the already-present true value.\n\n[The outer action wrapper](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/2024387a346bb88e0590e07cb3262e03307b997b/src/cli/main.ts#L1155-L1238) invokes registered handlers before its fallback; [positional validation](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/2024387a346bb88e0590e07cb3262e03307b997b/src/cli/main.ts#L1125-L1139) is restricted to importer/exporter commands. Free-form handlers intentionally receive context.args. As a dispatch control, the actual 10.13 canonical `type:\"boolean\"` echo handler already receives `truth:true,args:[\"false\"]` for `--truth false`, matching the path to which `bool` now normalizes.\n\nThe new probes use exact selected source modules with Node TypeScript erasure, real Commander and unchanged full invocation-options source, composed with existing 10.13 dependencies. This is not a build or installed-10.14 test.\n\n## Controls\n- `--enabled=false` and `--no-enabled` still produce false via the supported loose-option path.\n- Bare `--enabled` is newly accepted; old `bool` demanded an argument.\n- Unknown flags and missing required string values remain refused.\n- No real tracker or mutating extension action ran. Isolated HOME/PM path, telemetry disabled, network denied. All 6,411 baseline files remain byte-identical to the retained verified tarball.\n\n## Acceptance proposal\nPreserve the previously accepted explicitly valued alias invocation, or reject ambiguous trailing boolean literals before a handler can observe a contradictory option. Cover bare, equals-false, spaced false/0, negated and legitimate positional cases; do not silently reinterpret false as true. Confirm on the exact published artifact before release closure.\n\n## Ownership\nAll-status focused searches found no exact newer owner. Related completed work: #1461 / pm-gh1461 (inline flag help/identity normalization). This narrow follow-on does not reopen or negate its delivered fixes. No implementation is included."},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-14T07:56:00.352Z"}],"before_hash":"9b8ce261d287d51068d0e93639fd4e38040ae27a0743e54ab8b0e2ffed63ff4a","after_hash":"3246fdd485dd96d16ad1ec9e273d1db238fa4236e2b4bf08a49e271cc18f30e5","item_hash_version":3,"message":"Preserve complete source evidence and pending artifact acceptance","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"1c5f6a48796ece1ee0fb805e3630da8494476636ecee0969f4d813bdbc663071"}
